# Keep host build output out of the image context.
#
# Without this, `COPY backend/ backend/` drags in the developer's obj/ directories, whose
# project.assets.json records Windows NuGet paths (C:\Users\...\.nuget\packages). Inside the
# Linux build stage NuGet cannot resolve them and `dotnet publish` dies with MSB4018.
#
# CI never hits that — actions/checkout produces a clean tree — so the failure only ever shows up
# on a developer machine, which is exactly the kind of bug worth pinning down in a file.

# .NET build output
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Node / Angular build output and caches
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.angular/

# IDE and VCS
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/

# Docs and ops material: not needed to build the app, and they invalidate the build cache
# every time they change.
docs/
infra/
*.md
LICENSE

# Local compose file (production uses infra/docker-compose.yml)
docker-compose.yml
